  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1101 PM CDT SUN AUG 2 2026\n\nA dry slot has improved conditions across much of Central Alabama\nthis afternoon, though an unsettled pattern persists. We have\nhigh confidence that an upper-level trough will cut off into a\nclosed low over North Georgia by Monday afternoon. Moisture\nwrapping around this system will bring daily scattered showers\nand a low chance for thunderstorms, primarily in eastern areas,\nthrough midweek. Daytime high temperatures will trend slightly\ndownward through Tuesday as increased cloud cover inhibits full\nsun and afternoon heating.\n\nBy the end of the week, the low will weaken and move eastward,\nallowing heights to gradually rise across the region. This\ntransition will leave Alabama positioned between two high-\npressure systems, resulting in seasonal weekend conditions where\ntemperatures and daily convective rain chances align closely with\nhistorical averages for early August.\n\n16",
